        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "If you want to disagree with Tannen, you would probably choose the first version (note also the different verb):",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                117,
                772,
                167
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 2,
            "global_block_id": 2,
            "global_group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    117.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    117.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    167.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    167.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Linguist Deborah Tannen claims that our society's approach to argument is based on an assumption that competing positions and ideas must always be in conflict (284). But in fact, many in our society value different perspectives on complex issues.",
            "block_bbox": [
                114,
                180,
                743,
                280
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 3,
            "global_block_id": 3,
            "global_group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    114.0,
                    180.0
                ],
                [
                    743.0,
                    180.0
                ],
                [
                    743.0,
                    280.0
                ],
                [
                    114.0,
                    280.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "You need to attribute that first idea to someone else so you can disagree with it. If you don't, you might sound like you are contradicting yourself:",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                293,
                772,
                346
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 4,
            "global_block_id": 4,
            "global_group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    293.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    293.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    346.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    346.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Our society's approach to argument is based on an assumption that competing positions and ideas must always be in conflict (Tannen 284). But in fact, many in our society value different perspectives on complex issues.",
            "block_bbox": [
                110,
                358,
                743,
                432
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 5,
            "global_block_id": 5,
            "global_group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    110.0,
                    358.0
                ],
                [
                    743.0,
                    358.0
                ],
                [
                    743.0,
                    432.0
                ],
                [
                    110.0,
                    432.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "If you don't want to identify the author of your source by name, you can still attribute an idea generically:",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                445,
                770,
                496
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 6,
            "global_block_id": 6,
            "global_group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    445.0
                ],
                [
                    770.0,
                    445.0
                ],
                [
                    770.0,
                    496.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    496.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Some linguists claim that our society's approach to argument is based on an assumption that competing positions and ideas must always be in conflict (Tannen 284). But in fact, many in our society value different perspectives on complex issues.",
            "block_bbox": [
                114,
                509,
                742,
                609
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 7,
            "global_block_id": 7,
            "global_group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    114.0,
                    509.0
                ],
                [
                    742.0,
                    509.0
                ],
                [
                    742.0,
                    609.0
                ],
                [
                    114.0,
                    609.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Summing Up",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                646,
                253,
                680
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 8,
            "global_block_id": 8,
            "global_group_id": 8,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    646.0
                ],
                [
                    253.0,
                    646.0
                ],
                [
                    253.0,
                    680.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    680.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "You have ethical obligations to acknowledge words and ideas you borrow from others and to represent your sources accurately and fairly.",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                691,
                770,
                740
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 8,
            "group_id": 9,
            "global_block_id": 9,
            "global_group_id": 9,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    691.0
                ],
                [
                    770.0,
                    691.0
                ],
                [
                    770.0,
                    740.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    740.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Plagiarism, or using the words or ideas of others in ways that suggest they are your own, is a serious transgression. To avoid the appearance of plagiarism, follow this principle:",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                743,
                771,
                819
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 9,
            "group_id": 10,
            "global_block_id": 10,
            "global_group_id": 10,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    743.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    743.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    819.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    819.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- Avoid doing anything that might lead an informed reader to think that you are taking credit for words or ideas not your own.",
            "block_bbox": [
                91,
                827,
                770,
                876
            ],
            "block_id": 11,
            "block_order": 10,
            "group_id": 11,
            "global_block_id": 11,
            "global_group_id": 11,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    91.0,
                    827.0
                ],
                [
                    770.0,
                    827.0
                ],
                [
                    770.0,
                    876.0
                ],
                [
                    91.0,
                    876.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Follow these three reliable practices for giving credit to your sources:",
            "block_bbox": [
                80,
                885,
                666,
                909
            ],
            "block_id": 12,
            "block_order": 11,
            "group_id": 12,
            "global_block_id": 12,
            "global_group_id": 12,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    80.0,
                    885.0
                ],
                [
                    666.0,
                    885.0
                ],
                [
                    666.0,
                    909.0
                ],
                [
                    80.0,
                    909.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- When quoting from a source, put those words in quotation marks and cite the source according to the conventions of your field.",
            "block_bbox": [
                93,
                917,
                770,
                965
            ],
            "block_id": 13,
            "block_order": 12,
            "group_id": 13,
            "global_block_id": 13,
            "global_group_id": 13,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    93.0,
                    917.0
                ],
                [
                    770.0,
                    917.0
                ],
                [
                    770.0,
                    965.0
                ],
                [
                    93.0,
                    965.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- When paraphrasing a passage from a source, recast the passage entirely in your own words and cite the source according to the conventions of your field.",
            "block_bbox": [
                92,
                969,
                770,
                1018
            ],
            "block_id": 14,
            "block_order": 13,
            "group_id": 14,
            "global_block_id": 14,
            "global_group_id": 14,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    92.0,
                    969.0
                ],
                [
                    770.0,
                    969.0
                ],
                [
                    770.0,
                    1018.0
                ],
                [
                    92.0,
                    1018.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- When taking an idea or method from a source, cite the source according to the conventions of your field.",
            "block_bbox": [
                92,
                1021,
                771,
                1070
            ],
            "block_id": 15,
            "block_order": 14,
            "group_id": 15,
            "global_block_id": 15,
            "global_group_id": 15,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    92.0,
                    1021.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    1021.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    1070.0
                ],
                [
                    92.0,
                    1070.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Take notes in a way that ensures you will not mistake words or ideas from a source for your own words or ideas.",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                1079,
                770,
                1128
            ],
            "block_id": 16,
            "block_order": 15,
            "group_id": 16,
            "global_block_id": 16,
            "global_group_id": 16,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    1079.0
                ],
                [
                    770.0,
                    1079.0
                ],
                [
                    770.0,
                    1128.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    1128.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Punctuate and cite sources according to the conventions of your field. Understand the choices you have to make to use sources effectively:",
            "block_bbox": [
                111,
                1131,
                703,
                1181
            ],
            "block_id": 17,
            "block_order": 16,
            "group_id": 17,
            "global_block_id": 17,
            "global_group_id": 17,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    111.0,
                    1131.0
                ],
                [
                    703.0,
                    1131.0
                ],
                [
                    703.0,
                    1181.0
                ],
                [
                    111.0,
                    1181.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- How much of the source to include: Will you use just a word or phrase, a sentence, a passage, or a summary of the whole?",
            "block_bbox": [
                92,
                1189,
                771,
                1239
            ],
            "block_id": 18,
